+}

**Verifying browser zoom and viewport behavior**

I'm analyzing test coverage around native 200% browser zoom and how viewport sizes, device pixel ratios, and keyboard shortcuts behave—especially with Playwright in headless vs headed Chrome—and considering whether tests can fully verify UI and accessibility behavior under these conditions.
**Testing device metrics with CDP overrides**

I'm looking into how using Chrome DevTools Protocol to set device metrics with scale factors simulates 200% zoom by adjusting CSS pixels and device pixel ratio—but this isn’t the same as native browser zoom—and wondering why some Chrome APIs for font sizing or window bounds don't fully replicate actual browser zoom behavior.
